  "static_review": [
    "Only four implementation files plus two short required planning records; all source and prerequisite hashes unchanged during review.",
    "Reflection introspection and member splicing are confined to core.cpp. The public facade contains only fixed-width integers and has trivial-default, trivial-copy and standard-layout assertions.",
    "The smoke consumer links the actual library and compiles without -freflection; its preprocessor guard rejects leakage. Every generated compile command confirmed target-private reflection.",
    "CMake requires the qualified GCC16 toolchain and Ninja Multi-Config, C++26 without extensions, strict diagnostics, ARM64 and explicit SDK through the qualified toolchain.",
    "The MinSizeRel workaround only disables constructor/destructor decloning on the two targets. Language mode, exceptions and RTTI remain enabled. Pinned GCC manual and real red/fix/reverse controls support this scope.",
    "The harness records actual command return codes/log hashes, fails on an unexpected result, kills its owned process group on timeout/interruption, and checks protected state in finally. Timeout and interruption paths were reviewed statically only."
  ],
